From 9d696b3d591c7ce7b09ae0d4f6a9baa44c15fb94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openrazer-win contributor <contributor@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:18:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Studio: a visible low-battery warning

The notification was asked for in the same call that added its icon,
which Windows often answers with the icon alone. It now follows the
documented order: add the icon, set it to NOTIFYICON_VERSION_4, then
request the notification as its own step (warning icon, large).

A low battery also brings up a warning window: always on top at the
bottom centre of the main display's work area, for a time set in
Settings > System tray (10 s by default; a click closes it sooner),
independent of Windows' notification settings and Focus Assist. Drawn
as an egui immediate viewport, shown while the main window is parked in
the tray.
